\begin{align*}
t &= -\frac{b}{2a} \\
&= - \frac{32}{2 \times -16} \\
&= 1
\end{align*}
Instituting this into the given height equation to find the height:
\begin{align*}
-16t^2 + 32t + 15 &= - 16 (1)^2 + 32 (1) + 15 \\
&= 31
\end{align*}
Therefore, the maximum height of the ball is 31 feet.

